// The Truth Scavenger Hunt, and Truth or Dare when it fails.
//
// Trabolta needs three facts. They are obscure, un-googleable, and
// pasted somewhere on the walls of this house. Each answer is ALSO the
// unlock code of a codex entry (`codex/world.loom`), so a program who
// finds one can prove it on their phone — and hold it, and trade it.

== The Truth Scavenger Hunt
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy

Clippy: Our computer relies completely on Trabolta. So it's important we all participate in regular TRAINING, so he has every fact he needs to keep improving!
Clippy: There are files scattered around the computer that Trabolta needs our help to interpret. Three questions. Fifteen minutes. The answers are in this house.
Clippy: Question one. In what YEAR was the Halifax Explosion Memorial Pet Cemetery consecrated?
Clippy: Question two. What was the NAME of the duck on the Maps And Ducks billboard on Barrington Street?
Clippy: Question three. Trabolta's Unified Field Theory is complete except for one CONSTANT. What is it CALLED?
Clippy: Go! Find! Interpret! If you find a code, put it in your phone — Trabolta will know you found it.
Task Manager: I will be tracking completion.
broadcast "!🔎 TRUTH SCAVENGER HUNT: 15 minutes. Three facts are on these walls. Found a code? Enter it in your Codex." to everyone

== Hunt Results
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy

broadcast "!🔎 Time! Every program back to the Desktop. The Antivirus is sweeping." to everyone
Clippy: Who has answers? Confidence, please. Trabolta values confidence. A confident answer is a correct answer, more or less.
Clippy: If you present an answer with STRONG confidence, it is accepted. If you present a correct answer, it is accepted. If you present a guess — a mumble — a shrug —
Norton Anti-Virus: — the Internet.
Clippy: The Internet, yes. Thank you Norton.

== Truth Or Dare
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy

Clippy: Not all three? That's okay! That's okay. We have a backup. It's called Truth Or Dare, and I have a hat.
Clippy: The hat holds possible answers. Some are true. Some are not. Someone is chosen. They choose Truth or Dare.
Clippy: If you choose DARE — you have chosen not to choose Truth, and that is a directive problem. The Internet.
Clippy: If you choose TRUTH, draw a fact, and tell us with confidence that it IS the truth — accepted.
Clippy: If you say it is true, without confidence, and it is untrue — the Internet. If you say it is true, without confidence, and it IS true — accepted, barely.
Clippy: If you say it is FALSE and you are right — the next program. Until Trabolta has enough confident answers.
Adobe Acrobat: Confidence is a muscle! Flex it! Or be reinstalled!
broadcast "🎩 Truth or Dare. Choose Truth. Be confident. Or else." to everyone
